# Turnback Cave: a save inside a room (decomp FieldTask_LoadSavedGameMap). Loading runs no onTransition, so the
# room is not counted again and init_turnback_cave draws no new doors: the counters stay as saved and the doors
# keep the ROM's targets (the routing lives in the loaded map header, not in the save). A constructed start: one
# pillar seen and five rooms visited, the player at a pillar-1 room's south door; its onTransition adds the sixth.
set var platinum:VAR_TURNBACK_CAVE_PILLARS_SEEN 1
set var platinum:VAR_TURNBACK_CAVE_ROOMS_VISITED 5
warp platinum:MAP_HEADER_TURNBACK_CAVE_PILLAR_1_ROOM_1 11 20 up
until idle
+0 assert var platinum:VAR_TURNBACK_CAVE_ROOMS_VISITED 6
# save → load: the state must come back unchanged (the reload line fails on any difference).
+0 reload
until idle
+0 assert position platinum:MAP_HEADER_TURNBACK_CAVE_PILLAR_1_ROOM_1 11 20
+0 assert var platinum:VAR_TURNBACK_CAVE_PILLARS_SEEN 1
+0 assert var platinum:VAR_TURNBACK_CAVE_ROOMS_VISITED 6
# The east door (20,11): up a row, right to the aisle, up to the door's row, then right into it.
+0 press up
until position 11 19
+0 release up
+0 press right
until position 19 19
+0 release right
+0 press up
until position 19 11
+0 release up
+0 press right
until position 2 11 300
+0 release right
until idle 300
# The ROM's target: the entrance, whose onTransition clears both counters.
+0 assert position platinum:MAP_HEADER_TURNBACK_CAVE_ENTRANCE 2 11
+0 assert var platinum:VAR_TURNBACK_CAVE_PILLARS_SEEN 0
+0 assert var platinum:VAR_TURNBACK_CAVE_ROOMS_VISITED 0
